        "description_8VtDUT": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<p><strong>Truffles have a half-life of five days. It’s a ticking clock.</strong></p><p>Five days after harvest, half the aroma — that incomparable, irreplaceable perfume — is simply gone. By day ten, you're down to a quarter. By then, you're not getting a truffle. You're getting its memory.</p><p>Most European-produced truffles reach you 5 to 7 days after harvest, under the <em><strong>best</strong></em><strong> </strong>circumstances. And that's before you ask the question no one in the industry wants to answer: <em>Where exactly was this harvested? When? By whom? </em></p><p>They can't tell you. Because they don't know. That’s been the standard for decades.</p><p><strong>American Truffle Company® is changing all of that.</strong></p><p>We can't reveal too much – yet. We are still in stealth mode. But we <em>can </em>tell you this:</p><p><strong>A New Origin. Unprecedented Access. </strong>American-grown European black truffles. Farm to your door, overnight. Provenance you can trace. Freshness that redefines what a truffle is supposed to taste like.</p><p><em><strong>The freshest truffle available, anywhere. Period.</strong></em></p>"
